{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966800,"nonce":"7Q2PuT1hp6H6Z4wweNlsIETYaeI=","title":"refresh_stateful's queued subtree rebuilds clobber focused/hovered visuals via","message":"`refresh_stateful` → `refresh_props_internal` (in `stateful.rs`) does TWO things in one call when the on_state callback returns children: `queue_prop_update` (partial channel) AND one of `queue_subtree_rebuild` / `queue_layout_prop_subtree_rebuild` / `queue_visual_subtree_rebuild` (`PENDING_SUBTREE_REBUILDS`).\n\nEvery `process_pending_subtree_rebuilds` branch ends in `apply_stylesheet_base_styles_for_subtree` — Structural at [subtree.rs:434](crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/build/subtree.rs#L434), LayoutProps via `update_subtree_layout_from_builder` at [:583](crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/build/subtree.rs#L583), Visual via `update_subtree_props_from_builder` at [:663](crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/build/subtree.rs#L663). All three write the class-base CSS (`.cn-input { background: idle }`) on top of whatever the rebuild's temp_div produced, clobbering focused / hovered visuals.\n\nPhase 4's `apply_stylesheet_state_styles` is gated on `last_router_state_fp` changing between frames. On animation-tick / signal-refresh frames the router state is unchanged, the gate short-circuits, and `:focus` / `:hover` / `:active` are never re-applied on top of the just-clobbered base. The IDLE bg stays painted until a mouse-move bumps the fingerprint.\n\n**Why specifically cn::input and cn::textarea:**\n\n1. **Topology-changing on_state callback.** Both add the cursor canvas only when `visual.is_focused()`. Idle → Focused changes children → Structural rebuild path. cn::button / cn::checkbox typically only flip colours in their callback, so they hit the prop-update-only path and don't round-trip through the base-style clobber.\n2. **Deferred-queue focus.** Other Stateful widgets transition state via `POINTER_DOWN` inside `dispatch_event` — `refresh_stateful` fires DURING event dispatch, well before the first partial drain. cn::input / cn::textarea use `focus_text_input_deferred` / `focus_text_area_deferred` so focus runs AFTER the partial drain, which is what made the bug visible on first open.\n3. **Subsequent-frame clobbers.** Animation refresh chains (any Stateful spring tick, the cn-popover-enter that wraps the popover) keep firing `refresh_stateful` on later frames, each queuing a new rebuild → another clobber → another Phase 4 skip. That's the \"shows for one frame then disappears\" sequence.\n\n**Resolution:** `apply_stylesheet_base_styles_for_subtree` now takes `Option\u003c\u0026EventRouter\u003e`. When `Some`, after writing the base styles it calls a new helper `apply_state_styles_for_subtree(subtree_nodes, router)` ([selectors.rs:614+](crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/stylesheet/selectors.rs#L614)) which iterates `complex_rules.has_state()` × `subtree_nodes` (NOT all nodes — much cheaper than the global pass), saves `base_styles`, and writes matching `:focus` / `:hover` / `:active` rules on top of the base. Inserts touched nodes into `complex_state_affected` so the Phase 4 reset path still rolls them back correctly when the state actually clears.\n\n`process_pending_subtree_rebuilds` keeps its old signature for tests / mobile / web (which pass `None`); the routed variant `process_pending_subtree_rebuilds_routed(Some(\u0026router))` is what windowed.rs calls.\n\nThe fix runs ONCE per actual rebuild (regardless of which kind), restricted to the rebuilt subtree's nodes. No fingerprint-clearing band-aids, no inline Phase-4-style full passes, no `last_router_state_fp = None` regression of the steady-state-styles gate. Phase 4's gated pass keeps working as-is for the cases where the router state actually changes.\n\n**Caller responsibility:** when invoking the routed variant inline (e.g. after `process_pending_input_focus` drains and queues new rebuilds), sync `windowed_ctx.event_router.set_focus(focused_text_input_node_id())` BEFORE the routed rebuild so the in-pass `:focus` matching sees the correct focused node. The standard Phase 4 sync runs later in the frame and would be too late.\n\nRelated: [[gotcha-dropdown-hover-first-open]], [[gotcha-first-interaction-skips-class-animation]] — both also ride the `apply_stylesheet_state_styles` fingerprint gate; the same routed-base-pass would mitigate them when the trigger frame coincides with a subtree rebuild.","files":null}]}